# Presentation-golden corpus manifest.
#
# One row per bk2 sample set. presentation-corpus.sh captures, for each bk2,
# a canonical leg (tick-keyed) and an intermediate leg (deterministic alpha=0.5,
# VBL-keyed) on the native -vk path under llvmpipe. See
# notes/plans/openpete-presentation-golden.md.
#
# Fields (pipe-separated):
#   name         bk2 basename under games/spyro-1/bk2/ (its .args sidecar is
#                auto-spliced by the binary, so --skip-to-level etc. need not
#                be repeated here)
#   frame_limit  --frame-limit (VBLs); pick with margin over the last sample
#   canon_frames comma list of VBL frames for the canonical leg
#                (--screenshot-on-frame); start at the first frame %100==0 AFTER
#                the level finishes loading (g_Gamestate -> GS_Playing plus the
#                fade-in), then every 100 VBLs
#   inter_frames comma list of VBL frames for the alpha=0.5 intermediate leg
#                (--screenshot-intermediate-on-frame), offset +50 from the
#                canonical grid; each must fall in a stretch with a live interp
#                bracket (paired) — verify with the "paired=1" log line
#
# Bring-up is a single bk2 (cliff-town-vista, a far-terrain vista that exercises
# the depth fix's far-precision risk). It loads at f1197, goes GS_Playing at
# f1584, and the fade-in settles by ~f1650, so the corpus starts at f1700; the
# bk2 movie plays to ~f3990. Widen the set only once the pipeline is trusted
# end-to-end (see the plan's fan-out checklist item).
#
# name              | frame_limit | canon_frames (1700..3900 /100)                                                           | inter_frames (1750..3950 /100)
cliff-town-vista    | 4200        | 1700,1800,1900,2000,2100,2200,2300,2400,2500,2600,2700,2800,2900,3000,3100,3200,3300,3400,3500,3600,3700,3800,3900 | 1750,1850,1950,2050,2150,2250,2350,2450,2550,2650,2750,2850,2950,3050,3150,3250,3350,3450,3550,3650,3750,3850,3950
